# .spool/coverage.req

feature: COVERAGE

requirements:

  - id: COVERAGE-1
    title: Report Format Flag
    description: >
      `spool` takes a --format flag that chooses how the whole-repo report
      is printed: text, json or markdown. Text stays the default.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-06
    rationale: >
      The reporter has shipped JSON and markdown formatters since
      REPORTER-4 and REPORTER-5, but the CLI always prints text, so a
      script has to scrape the text table. The slice verifier and CI
      both need output they can parse.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Writing the report to a file (REPORTER-6's destination stays unused
        by the CLI)
      - Flags for `spool init` and `spool lsp`
      - Changing the JSON or markdown formatters' output
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: COVERAGE-1-1
        title: Text by Default
        description: >
          Given a project and no flags,
          when spool runs,
          then it prints the same text report as before and exits with
          the same status.

      - id: COVERAGE-1-2
        title: JSON Report
        description: >
          Given --format json,
          when spool runs,
          then stdout holds the JSON formatter's output for the whole
          report and nothing else, and the exit status follows the
          configured severities as it does for text.

      - id: COVERAGE-1-3
        title: Markdown Report
        description: >
          Given --format markdown,
          when spool runs,
          then stdout holds the markdown formatter's output for the
          whole report, and the exit status follows the configured
          severities as it does for text.

      - id: COVERAGE-1-4
        title: Usage Errors
        description: >
          Given an unknown --format value, an unknown flag, or an
          unexpected argument,
          when spool runs,
          then it prints a message naming the problem to stderr, prints
          nothing to stdout, and exits 2.

    invariants:

      - id: COVERAGE-1-INV-1
        title: Stdout Holds Only the Report
        description: >
          Whatever the flags and whatever the project contains, parse,
          scan and index warnings, errors and usage messages go to
          stderr, so stdout is either empty or exactly one report in the
          requested format.

  - id: COVERAGE-2
    title: Coverage for Listed IDs
    description: >
      `spool --ids <ID>,<ID>,...` reports, for each listed AC or invariant,
      whether it has a linked test and which tests those are, and exits
      non-zero when any of them is untested or unknown. It ignores the
      rest of the repo.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-06
    rationale: >
      The slice verifier must check that a slice's own ACs and invariants
      are covered. The whole-repo report can't answer that: it fails on
      unrelated untested items elsewhere, and passes a slice whose item
      is untested when untested_ac is set below error. A listed ID is
      required to be covered whatever the configured severities, because
      listing it is the requirement. Test files are reported relative to
      the project root, so output from a container and from the host
      match.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Expanding a requirement ID to its ACs and invariants
      - Checking the status of a listed ID's requirement (per-item status
        is Spool foundations item 3)
      - Reading the IDs from a file or from stdin
      - A markdown format for listed IDs
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: COVERAGE-2-1
        title: Listed IDs Reported
        description: >
          Given --ids with AC and invariant IDs,
          when spool runs,
          then it prints one entry per ID in the order given, with each
          ID normalized and listed once even if repeated. An entry gives
          the ID, its state (covered, untested or unknown) and, for each
          linked test, the test file relative to the project root, the
          line and the function name. The text format prints the ID and
          state on one line, each test indented on its own line below as
          `<file>:<line> <function>`, and a last line `<n>/<m> covered`.

      - id: COVERAGE-2-2
        title: All Covered Passes
        description: >
          Given --ids whose IDs all have at least one linked test,
          when spool runs,
          then it exits 0, even if other ACs or invariants in the repo are
          untested, annotations are orphaned, and those findings are set
          to error.

      - id: COVERAGE-2-3
        title: Untested Fails
        description: >
          Given --ids where at least one ID has no linked test,
          when spool runs,
          then it still reports every listed ID and exits 1, even if
          untested_ac and untested_invariant are set to warning, info or
          off.

      - id: COVERAGE-2-4
        title: Unknown Fails
        description: >
          Given --ids with a well-formed AC or invariant ID that no .req
          file defines,
          when spool runs,
          then that ID is reported as unknown with no tests and spool
          exits 1.

      - id: COVERAGE-2-5
        title: Bad ID List
        description: >
          Given --ids with an empty list, an empty item, a malformed ID,
          or a requirement ID such as SLICE-8,
          when spool runs,
          then it prints a message naming the bad item to stderr, prints
          nothing to stdout, and exits 2.

      - id: COVERAGE-2-6
        title: JSON for Listed IDs
        description: >
          Given --ids and --format json,
          when spool runs,
          then stdout holds one JSON object with "ids", a list of
          {"id", "kind" ("ac", "invariant" or "unknown"), "covered",
          "tests"} where each test is {"file", "line", "function"} and
          "tests" is [] rather than null when there are none, plus
          "covered" and "total" counts. Given --ids and --format
          markdown, spool exits 2 as a usage error.
